--
--  The frozen Cauchy generator matrix for the Reed-Solomon code.
--
--  C (i, j) = 1 / (x_i XOR y_j)  in GF(2^8),  with
--     y_j = j - 1        for j in 1 .. 32   ->  0 .. 31   (data columns)
--     x_i = 32 + i - 1   for i in 1 .. 32   ->  32 .. 63  (parity rows)
--
--  The two index sets are disjoint by construction, so x_i XOR y_j is never
--  zero and the reciprocal always exists.  EVERY square submatrix of a Cauchy
--  matrix is invertible -- that is the property that makes the erasure code
--  MDS: ANY K surviving fragments out of N reconstruct the data, with no
--  special cases and no unlucky combinations.
--
--  Frozen rather than computed, for the same reason as the GF tables: nothing
--  to prove about its construction, and a human can check it.

with Gf256; use Gf256;

